A||||7||SLYGUY||Unusual Clutch prob....||||5||
Z||000000||SLYGUY||11-30-2001||03:40 AM||||I thought I had the clutch problem licked but here goes:<P>I had a problem with disengagement. Turned out to be a shot master cylinder. Replaced it with a new GM unit and bled it. All seemed well despite a not so thorough bleeding. <P>Disengagement is fine until I run the car over 50mph for 10+ minutes. Then the point of disengagement creeps closer and closer to the floor. Bleeding the system with my Mityvac results in more and more air and the clutch is once again restored.<P>Question is:<BR>Do I need to search the entire system for a tiny pinhole leak (AARRGHHH!!) or could it be a dying slave cylinder? <BR>Just how much air should I expect to pull from this thing?<P>Thank you in advance for your ideas!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||11-30-2001||11:52 AM||||sounds like your on the correct track. "search for a pin hole leak" or slave.  The air should not continue to "develop"||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||11-30-2001||11:56 AM||||Yep.  Your slave is on its last legs.  I have a new GM slave cylinder.....cheaper than one from a dealer.  LMK if you are interested and we'll talk price.<P> As for the amount of air......not much.  If the master and slave were in perfect working condition (no leaks) then 2 or 3 pumps is sufficient to remove all of the air.  <P>Try bleeding the slave cylinder first, before replacing it, and see what happens.  Maybe you just have an air pocket inside the slave (not likely, but possible).<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DR650SE||11-30-2001||12:32 PM||||I had a similiar problem.  I had a slave taht had a hairline crack.  It would suck air in but not let fluid out.  Must have been small.  Anyway I found this bleeding.  The side of the valve broke.  I still have yet to get a replacement.  Go GM parts on the slave.  Mine was an aftermarket slave with very very little miles on it and look what happened.  Good Luck.   Keep us updated.<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DR650SEsig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||11-30-2001||02:38 PM||||Thanks for all of your help.<P>I've never bled the slave. I use the car daily, but I'll replace the slave very soon now. Now all that's left is the throwout bearing, which will be replaced in the next few months along with both the friction/pressure plates!!!!<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||ssalyers||11-30-2001||06:49 PM||||I recently went through this too.  I couldn't find an OE master & slave at a decent price so I went aftermarket.  A local parts chain (Bennett Auto Supply) sells Bendix hydraulic parts.  I bought the slave and master in Bendix.  Come to find out, Raybestos makes the AC Delco slaves & masters for them.  The Bendix units I bought were supposedly "redisgned to correct factory flaws".  Well, I have a firmer and better feeling pedal than I've ever seen in any of the Fieros I've owned.  Even reverse is not a problem!!  The slave was about an 1" longer than the factory unit.<P>Just my 2 cents!!!<P>--Shawn||||reg||3
Z||000006||TRiAD||11-30-2001||08:50 PM||||ssalyers, how much?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||SLYGUY||12-01-2001||03:41 AM||||Update:<P>I went ahead and bled the system some more and the problem went away. The problem is that it always does this. <P>Exiting the freeway I anxiously depressed the clutch pedal expecting it to feel lousy and the clutch to disengage just off the floor and it felt just fine. Felt every bit as good as in the driveway over 1/2 hour earlier. I didn't expect this. <P>Does anyone else have a clutch that grabs 2-3 inches from the floor? This is weird. That is gonna take some getting used to. I like the whole engagement thing to happen closer to the floor but if having this all take place farther up is the tradeoff for full disengagement than I'll buy it. <P>Fiero clutches are a finicky sort. Sounds like bad engineering until you remember just how much hydraulic line is wound between the master cylinder and the slave itself.<P>Still love the car anyways. How about you guys?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||1
